{"id": "EUVD-2026-102285", "enisaUuid": "5d9fdd13-d362-3acd-9182-59c6b2b2227e", "description": "EarthScope libmseed through 3.5.4 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in ms3_detect() in parseutils.c that reads past truncated miniSEED 2 record buffers. Attackers can supply a 40 to 47 byte buffer passing MS2_ISVALIDHEADER to msr3_parse() or ms3_detect(), over-reading up to 8 bytes and potentially crashing the process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:42:14", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libmseed-ms3detect-short-header-oob-read", "https://github.com/EarthScope/libmseed/blob/d6e6ad306de5b7bdde072e5a5e3d58ddcc11abd8/parseutils.c#L192-L234", "https://github.com/EarthScope/libmseed/commit/c93a36a1381e944b59b10967342ee1cb94304223", "https://github.com/EarthScope/libmseed", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/earthscope-libmseed-through-3.5.4-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-ms3-detect"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p3hv-2xrm-x5px", "CVE-2026-111158"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "60eb1dba-ce7b-3da3-8727-d0b3503fc048", "product": {"name": "libmseed", "vendor": {"name": "EarthScope"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.5.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0ffca437-980a-3dc4-8746-52495ac1b2fd", "vendor": {"name": "EarthScope"}}], "isExploited": false}